# Dialog buttons: one layout everywhere

Put a dialog's buttons in `DialogActions` (`@/components/common/DialogActions`), main action last:

- Wider screens: right-aligned, main action rightmost.
- Phones: stacked full width, main action on top.

```tsx
<DialogActions>
  <PracticeButton variant="secondary" onClick={onCancel}>Cancel</PracticeButton>
  <PracticeButton variant="danger" onClick={onDelete}>Delete</PracticeButton>
</DialogActions>
```

A screen with a single way out ("You're logged out" → Close) uses one full-width `PracticeButton size="md"` instead. Low-key extras ("Reset to defaults") go in the dialog body as a `TextActionButton`, not in the button row.
